# The map file (W1b): what a map holds, from its header and its tiles, and files that aren't one.

# A hand-made map of 70 × 66 tiles, with three overrides; its summary is two lines, so the
# snapshot checks it.
world info crates/content/tests/fixtures/maps/hand-made.map

# Its suggestions (W6b), with poi_0 dismissed, and route_7 dismissed though it isn't on the map
# (W6c): a dismissal is kept whatever's suggested now. The session's tests assert the listing.
world suggestions crates/content/tests/fixtures/maps/hand-made.map

assert world info content/sample/factions.toml == error: this isn't a Factional map
assert world info == error: world needs the form: world info <file>, world source <file>, world suggestions <map>, world dismiss <map> <id> [<id>…], world restore <map> <id> [<id>…], or world import <export> <map> [--region <x>,<y>,<width>,<height>] [--scale <n>] [--seed <n>] [--detail <strength>] [--wavelength <pixels>] [--octaves <n>] [--shallows <metres>] [--specks <tiles>] [--levels <points>] [--level-specks <tiles>] [--foliage <scale>] [--tree-spacing <tiles>] [--shrub-spacing <tiles>] [--grass-spacing <tiles>]
